[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: IRONAIR-MATLAB Equation Requirements
UID: DOC-IRONAIR-EQUATIONS
VERSION: 1.0.0

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-001
TITLE: Primary iron oxidation and reduction
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.1
| 
| Reaction:
| 
| '''text
| Fe + 2OH_minus <-> FeOH2 + 2e_minus
| '''
| 
| This is the primary reversible iron-storage reaction.
| 
| The reaction SHALL be represented in the central stoichiometric matrix.
| 
| Oxidation is positive in the discharge direction.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.1
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-002
TITLE: Iron electrode equilibrium potential
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirements: SRS003.1, SRS019
| 
| '''matlab
| e_Fe_eq = e_Fe_std + ...
|     (R_J_molK .* T_Fe ./ (2 .* F_C_mol)) .* ...
|     log(a_FeOH2 ./ (a_Fe .* a_OH.^2));
| '''
| 
| For pure, coexisting Fe and FeOH2 solids, their activities MAY equal unity.
| 
| Activity conventions and standard potentials SHALL use consistent reference states.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.1
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS019
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-003
TITLE: Iron Butler-Volmer kinetics
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.2
| 
| '''matlab
| j_Fe = j_0_Fe .* ( ...
|     exp(alpha_a_Fe .* 2 .* F_C_mol .* eta_Fe ./ ...
|         (R_J_molK .* T_Fe)) ...
|     - exp(-alpha_c_Fe .* 2 .* F_C_mol .* eta_Fe ./ ...
|         (R_J_molK .* T_Fe)) ...
| );
| '''
| 
| The implementation SHALL support stable exponent evaluation.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.2
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-004
TITLE: Iron electrode overpotential
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.2
| 
| '''matlab
| eta_Fe = phi_s_Fe - phi_l_Fe - e_Fe_eq;
| '''
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.2
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-005
TITLE: Iron Faradaic current
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.2
| 
| '''matlab
| I_Fe = A_active_Fe .* j_Fe;
| '''
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.2
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-006
TITLE: Temperature-dependent exchange current
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.2
| 
| '''matlab
| j_0_Fe_T = j_0_Fe_ref .* exp( ...
|     -(E_a_Fe ./ R_J_molK) .* ...
|     (1 ./ T_Fe - 1 ./ T_ref_K) ...
| );
| '''
| 
| Additional composition and phase-availability factors SHALL be included in the detailed kinetic model.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.2
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-007
TITLE: Metallic iron inventory derivative
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirements: SRS003.3, SRS023
| 
| '''matlab
| dn_Fe_dt = -I_Fe ./ (2 .* F_C_mol);
| '''
| 
| This isolated-reaction equation SHALL be extended with all other iron-producing or iron-consuming pathways.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: conservation law
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS023
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-008
TITLE: Ferrous hydroxide inventory derivative
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirements: SRS003.3, SRS023
| 
| '''matlab
| dn_FeOH2_dt = I_Fe ./ (2 .* F_C_mol);
| '''
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: conservation law
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS023
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-009
TITLE: Iron utilization
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.3
| 
| '''matlab
| U_Fe = 1 - n_Fe ./ n_Fe_initial;
| '''
| 
| Valid for a defined initially metallic iron reference inventory.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: conservation law
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-010
TITLE: Electrode porosity
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.3
| 
| '''matlab
| epsilon_Fe = 1 - ...
|     sum(n_solid .* V_molar_solid) ./ V_electrode;
| '''
| 
| All solid constituents, including inert structure where applicable, SHALL be accounted for.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-011
TITLE: Effective active surface area
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.3
| 
| '''matlab
| A_active_Fe = A_geometric_Fe .* a_s_Fe .* ...
|     f_wet_Fe .* f_pass_Fe .* f_availability_Fe;
| '''
| 
| 'a_s_Fe' SHALL be a dimensionless area multiplier in this expression. If using specific surface area in m2/m3, the expression SHALL be reformulated dimensionally.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-012
TITLE: Passivation layer dynamics
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirements: SRS003.3, SRS016
| 
| '''matlab
| ddelta_pass_dt = ...
|     k_pass_growth .* abs(j_Fe).^m_pass ...
|     - k_pass_removal .* g_pass_removal;
| '''
| 
| This is an empirical model requiring calibration.
| 
| The function 'g_pass_removal' SHALL depend on relevant electrode potential, temperature, and electrolyte conditions.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: empirical approximation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS016
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-013
TITLE: Passivation resistance
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirements: SRS003.3, SRS016
| 
| '''matlab
| R_pass = delta_pass ./ ...
|     (sigma_pass .* A_effective_pass);
| '''
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS016
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-014
TITLE: Magnetite formation reaction
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirements: SRS003.1, SRS003.3
| 
| '''text
| 3FeOH2 + 2OH_minus <-> Fe3O4 + 4H2O + 2e_minus
| '''
| 
| This reaction SHALL be optional and separately parameterized.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.1
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-015
TITLE: Magnetite production rate
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.3
| 
| '''matlab
| dn_Fe3O4_dt = I_mag ./ (2 .* F_C_mol);
| '''
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: conservation law
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS003.3
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_metal_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FE-016
TITLE: Ferrous hydroxide consumption by magnetite formation
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS003.3
| 
| '''matlab
| dn_FeOH2_dt_mag = ...
|     -3 .* I_mag ./ (2 .* F_C_mol);
| '''
| 
| The complete iron phase derivatives SHALL be assembled from all relevant reaction contributions.
| 
| ---
| 
