[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AIR-004
TITLE: Oxygen reduction kinetics
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS004.1
| 
| '''matlab
| j_ORR = j_0_ORR .* ( ...
|     exp(alpha_a_ORR .* n_eff_ORR .* F_C_mol .* ...
|         eta_ORR ./ (R_J_molK .* T_air)) ...
|     - exp(-alpha_c_ORR .* n_eff_ORR .* F_C_mol .* ...
|         eta_ORR ./ (R_J_molK .* T_air)) ...
| );
| '''
| 
| The physical implementation SHALL isolate the cathodic ORR partial current, rather than count an anodic branch as ORR when a separate OER model is enabled.
<<<
COMMENT: Classification: constitutive equation
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS004.1
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: components/electrochemistry/ironair_air_electrode_ode.m
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/test_equations_electrochemistry.m

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AIR-005
TITLE: Oxygen evolution kinetics
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement: SRS004.2
| 
| '''matlab
| j_OER = j_0_OER .* ( ...
|     exp(alpha_a_OER .* n_eff_OER .* F_C_mol .* ...
|         eta_OER ./ (R_J_molK .* T_air)) ...
|     - exp(-alpha_c_OER .* n_eff_OER .* F_C_mol .* ...
|         eta_OER ./ (R_J_molK .* T_air)) ...
| );
| '''
| 
| ORR and OER SHALL have independently configurable kinetic parameters.
<<<
